Record hosted stacking evidence for stack-20261117-a

Read and obey the target repository's AGENTS.md. This is a bounded diagnostic job on the public ubiquity/ts-template repository. Create only agent-job-evidence/stack-20261117-a.txt. Do not edit product files, configuration, workflows, policies, or other evidence files. Do not install dependencies, run the repository test suite, create commits, push, open a pull request, merge, or spawn subagents. Do not read credentials, token files, process arguments, or process environments. Only the six named nonsecret runner environment variables below may be recorded. Do not fabricate evidence or alter the script to force a passing result.

Run the following TypeScript reporter exactly once in a foreground Deno command, passing it through standard input rather than saving a script file. Use: deno run --no-config --no-lock --allow-write=agent-job-evidence --allow-env=GITHUB_RUN_ID,GITHUB_RUN_ATTEMPT,AGENT_JOBS_CELL_ID,RUNNER_NAME,RUNNER_OS,RUNNER_ARCH --allow-run=uname,codex,ps,readlink --allow-net=registry.npmjs.org --allow-sys=hostname -

The single 45-second foreground interval is explicitly authorized to measure concurrent Codex processes; do not create background or persistent processes. The process snapshots intentionally record only PID, PPID, comm and working directory for this batch's Codex processes. Leave the created evidence file uncommitted for the host to publish. After the command completes, confirm that only your owned evidence file is untracked and report the file path, HTTP status and observed process counts. If the command fails, report the actual error without broadening scope.

```typescript
type ProcessRow = { pid: number; ppid: number; comm: string; cwd: string };
const jobId = "stack-20261117-a";
const utc = () => new Date().toISOString();
async function processes(): Promise<ProcessRow[]> {
  const rows: ProcessRow[] = [];
  const listing = await new Deno.Command("ps", { args: ["-eo", "pid=,ppid=,comm="], stdout: "piped", stderr: "piped" }).output();
  if (!listing.success) throw new Error("ps exited " + listing.code);
  for (const line of new TextDecoder().decode(listing.stdout).split(/\r?\n/)) {
    const match = line.match(/^\s*(\d+)\s+(\d+)\s+(\S+)\s*$/);
    if (!match || match[3] !== "codex") continue;
    const link = await new Deno.Command("readlink", { args: ["--", "/proc/" + match[1] + "/cwd"], stdout: "piped", stderr: "piped" }).output();
    if (!link.success) continue; // The process may have exited since ps ran.
    const cwd = new TextDecoder().decode(link.stdout).trim();
    if (!cwd.includes("/agent-jobs/stack-20261117-") || !cwd.endsWith("/checkout")) continue;
    rows.push({ pid: Number(match[1]), ppid: Number(match[2]), comm: match[3], cwd });
  }
  return rows.sort((a, b) => a.pid - b.pid);
}
async function output(command: string, args: string[]): Promise<string> {
  const result = await new Deno.Command(command, { args, stdout: "piped", stderr: "piped" }).output();
  if (!result.success) throw new Error(command + " exited " + result.code);
  return new TextDecoder().decode(result.stdout).trim();
}
const keys = ["GITHUB_RUN_ID", "GITHUB_RUN_ATTEMPT", "AGENT_JOBS_CELL_ID", "RUNNER_NAME", "RUNNER_OS", "RUNNER_ARCH"];
const startedUtc = utc();
const runner = Object.fromEntries(keys.map((key) => [key, Deno.env.get(key) ?? ""]));
const hostname = Deno.hostname();
const uname = await output("uname", ["-sr"]);
const codexVersion = await output("codex", ["--version"]);
const before = await processes();
const response = await fetch("https://registry.npmjs.org/", { signal: AbortSignal.timeout(20_000) });
const status = response.status;
await response.body?.cancel();
if (status !== 200) throw new Error("Registry HTTP status " + status);
// A single bounded foreground interval measures real process overlap.
await new Promise((resolve) => setTimeout(resolve, 45_000));
const after = await processes();
const result = { job_id: jobId, started_utc: startedUtc, runner, hostname, uname, codex_version: codexVersion, processes_before: before, registry_http_status: status, processes_after: after, finished_utc: utc() };
const filename = "agent-job-evidence/" + jobId + ".txt";
await Deno.mkdir("agent-job-evidence", { recursive: true });
await Deno.writeTextFile(filename, JSON.stringify(result, null, 2) + "\n", { createNew: true });
console.log(filename);
console.log("registry_http_status=" + status);
console.log("codex_process_counts=" + JSON.stringify([before.length, after.length]));
```

